cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HydroGrad (the dgga package) in your work, please cite the
  software record below and the accompanying paper.
  Cite the archived version you used (Zenodo); the concept DOI below always
  resolves to the latest version.
type: software
title: "HydroGrad: a differentiable global gradient algorithm with implicit adjoint sensitivities for EPANET 2.2 models"
abstract: >-
  HydroGrad (Python package dgga) implements the global gradient algorithm of
  EPANET 2.2, including its status logic, in PyTorch, and makes the steady
  state differentiable with respect to demands, pipe resistances, reservoir
  heads, pump curve coefficients and emitter (leak) coefficients through an
  implicit adjoint and an unrolled route. It adds a batched status machine, a
  sparse batched GPU route (cuDSS) and a GPU implicit adjoint that reuses the
  forward factorisation.
